==Company activities==
===Cultural promotion===
In September 2020, miHoYo established strategic cooperation with [[Zhangjiajie]]  to promote cultural tourism in the city with the help of ''Genshin Impact''. The topography of Zhangjiajie's karst landscapes inspired the level designs of Jueyun Karst and Mt. Tianheng. After the agreement, two life-size Teleport Waypoints were installed at the [[Zhangjiajie National Forest Park]] and Huangshi Village ({{lang|zh|黄石寨}}).<ref>{{Cite web |title=米哈游×张家界：文旅合作新探索 |url=https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100603 |access-date=29 July 2022 |website=mihoyo.com |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124432/https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100603 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Hu |first=Yuanyuan |date=2020-09-23 |title=打造游戏打卡地，张家界探索文旅合作新方向 |url=https://baijiahao.baidu.com/s?id=1678615697029937610&wfr=spider&for=pc |url-status=live |access-date=2026-05-10 |work=Sanxiang Metropolis Daily|trans-title=Zhangjiajie Builds 'Checkpoints' and Explore New Directions of Collaboration between Culture and Tourism|language=zh|via=Baidu}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |author=原神 |date=25 September 2020 |title=《原神》「从驻足到远行」线下活动圆满结束(๑•̀ㅂ•́)و✧ |url=https://t.bilibili.com/438625802849156411 |access-date=3 August 2022 |website=Bilibili |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124432/https://t.bilibili.com/438625802849156411 |url-status=live }}</ref> Next, miHoYo cooperated with [[Huanglong Scenic and Historic Interest Area|Huanglong]] for ecological environment protection. Huanglong's multicolored pools served as the inspiration for the level design of Luhua Pool in [[Liyue, Teyvat|Liyue]].<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=30 November 2020 |title=米哈游×黄龙：赋能生态环境保护 |url=https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100605 |access-date=29 July 2022 |website=mihoyo.com |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124436/https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100605 |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Charity and aid===
In November 2020, miHoYo and the [[China Social Welfare Foundation]] ({{lang|zh|中国社会福利基金会}}) jointly launched the [[Yiqi Shouhu]] ({{lang|zh|弈起守护}}) charity program. During the event, all profits from ''Tears of Themis'' charity gift packs were donated to the foundation as relief for children with autism.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=20 November 2020 |title=米哈游携手中国社会福利基金会：守护"星星的孩子" |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/uhcdq4FMlbaHF555P9DM8w |access-date=31 July 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124433/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/uhcdq4FMlbaHF555P9DM8w |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 12 July 2021, the [[Xinhuo Charity Program]] ({{lang|zh|薪火公益计划}}) was jointly launched by the [[China Youth Development Foundation]] and Shanghai Mihoyo Network Technology Co., Ltd. The project is committed to paying attention to and supporting the development of youth education. The first phase involved Tongzi Primary School ({{lang|zh|桐梓小学}}) in [[Yunnan|Yunnan Province]], which got support from various aspects such as hardware conditions, educational facilities, teacher training, etc. The project also aims to provide school uniforms for all students and launch a teacher training program for seventeen primary schools in [[Yanjin County, Yunnan|Yanjin County]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=希望不熄 薪火永燃｜中国青基会与米哈游成立薪火公益计划 |url=https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100594 |access-date=29 July 2022 |website=mihoyo.com |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124434/https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100594 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |author=米哈游miHoYo |date=12 July 2021 |title=「薪火公益计划」首站纪录片 |url=https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV18g411T7nH |access-date=11 August 2022 |website=Bilibili |archive-date=2 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220802113843/https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV18g411T7nH/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 23 July 2021, miHoYo delivered disaster relief supplies to [[Xinmi|Xinmi County]] in [[Henan|Henan Province]]. Henan Province experienced flooding due to heavy rainfall, affecting hundreds of people.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=23 July 2021 |title=紧急驰援河南！米哈游首批救灾物资预计今日抵达！ |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/PvEZXN2PmELw12NoCAQz1A |access-date=3 August 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124438/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/PvEZXN2PmELw12NoCAQz1A |url-status=live }}</ref>

In February 2022, [[2022 Shanghai COVID-19 outbreak|Shanghai experienced a COVID-19 outbreak]] that led to a city-wide lockdown until June. In March, miHoYo responded to the critical stage of the epidemic control by purchasing batches of supplies and donating them to the Caohejing ({{lang|zh|漕河泾}}) and Hongmei ({{lang|zh|虹梅}}) communities in Xuhui District. In April, the second batch of supplies included 10,000 sets of protective equipment, 10,000 bottles of hand sanitizer gel, 40,000 [[N95 respirator|N95]] masks, and 100,000 pieces of disinfection wipes.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=20 April 2022 |title=战"疫"有我，共克时艰 ——米哈游再次捐赠防疫物资，助力疫情防控 |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/2hlcw6i18ByL5oQGUmVo1A |access-date=31 July 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124437/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/2hlcw6i18ByL5oQGUmVo1A |url-status=live }}</ref> miHoYo also donated pillows and peripheral products for children at a makeshift hospital at Shilong Road ({{lang|zh|石龙路}}). In response to employees' needs, the company distributed food packages and epidemic prevention supplies to employees affected by the lockdown. The packages included fruits, vegetables, and disinfection and protection materials. Also provided were mental health counseling services.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游招聘 |date=25 April 2022 |title=米哈游er抗疫切片 |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/Nb5pPpcnI9x81toQgE_d4A |access-date=1 August 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124432/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/Nb5pPpcnI9x81toQgE_d4A |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 15 August 2022, miHoYo released a video about the second phase of the Xinhuo Charity Program, which showed the completed construction of Tongzi Primary School's new building from the first phase. Students can study in the multimedia classrooms of the building with upgraded hardware. Furthermore, new street lamps were installed on the campus for the safety of the students at night. The second phase also included the construction of a waterway, flush toilet, bathroom, and solar-powered water stations for the student and staff dormitory in Bazha Village Central Primary School ({{lang|zh|巴扎乡中心学校}}) in [[Qinghai|Qinghai Province]]. The construction expects completion in the second half of 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |author=米哈游miHoYo |date=15 August 2022 |title=「薪火公益计划」第二站纪录片 |url=https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1Je4y1f7Qe |access-date=16 August 2022 |website=Bilibili |archive-date=15 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220815110614/https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1Je4y1f7Qe/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

In November 2022, miHoYo collaborated with the Taofen Foundation ({{lang|zh|韬奋基金会}}) to jointly launch the Yuejian Weiming ({{lang|zh|阅见未名}}) charity project. More than 37,000 books worth 2 million Yuan were donated to a number of primary schools in [[Dali Bai Autonomous Prefecture]] and [[Lancang Lahu Autonomous County]] of Yunnan Province. Aside from books, postcards written by ''Tears of Themis'' players were also given to students.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=24 November 2022 |title="你们好，见字如面！"——「阅见未名：图书捐赠公益活动」进展 |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/-u9Vsmxi6Rz21a_7r8Zn6w |access-date=25 November 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=25 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221125083418/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/-u9Vsmxi6Rz21a_7r8Zn6w |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |author=韬奋基金会 |date=23 November 2022 |title="你们好，见字如面！"——米哈游《未定事件簿》与韬奋基金会共同向云南省两地小学捐赠爱心书籍并写信问候  |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/eTwA2ZVlbtfU7AxZHFQtxg |access-date=25 November 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=25 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221125084028/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/eTwA2ZVlbtfU7AxZHFQtxg |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Investments===
On 4 March 2021, miHoYo signed an agreement of strategic cooperation with [[Ruijin Hospital]] to build the miHoYo Joint Laboratory of Encephalopathy Center of Ruijin Hospital ({{lang|zh|瑞金医院脑病中心米哈游联合实验室}}), also called the Ruijin-miHoYo Laboratory.<ref>{{Cite web |title=米哈游与上海交大的联合实验室，披露了部分在研项目 |url=https://www.sohu.com/a/522149265_204824 |access-date=30 July 2022 |website=Sohu |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124432/https://www.sohu.com/a/522149265_204824 |url-status=live }}</ref> The two parties would combine their respective advantages in medical research and information technology to jointly develop brain-computer interface technology research. Lü Baoliang ({{lang|zh|吕宝粮}}), a professor from the Department of Computer Science and Engineering of Shanghai Jiao Tong University, heads the laboratory; he was also the supervisor of miHoYo co-founder Cai Haoyu's master's thesis. The laboratory began with the research project "Clinical Research on Brain-Computer Interface Neuromodulation and Treatment of Refractory Depression."<ref>{{Cite news |author=文化观澜 |date=4 March 2021 |title=爆款游戏《原神》出品公司米哈游与瑞金医院成立脑科学联合实验室，攻关难治性抑郁症 |url=https://www.shobserver.com/staticsg/res/html/web/newsDetail.html?id=346777 |access-date=28 July 2022 |website=Shanghai Observer |archive-date=26 January 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220126133507/https://www.shobserver.com/staticsg/res/html/web/newsDetail.html?id=346777 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |author=李劲湘 |date=9 March 2021 |title=附属瑞金医院与上海米哈游网络科技股份有限公司签约合作 |url=https://news.sjtu.edu.cn/jdyw/20210306/142715.html |access-date=30 July 2022 |website=上海交通大学新闻学术网 |archive-date=29 January 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220129041314/https://news.sjtu.edu.cn/jdyw/20210306/142715.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

In early 2022, miHoYo and NIO Capital led the first funding round for Energy Singularity, raising nearly CNY 400 million. Energy Singularity was established in 2021 in Shanghai, China. The company focuses on the research and development of [[High-temperature superconductivity|HTS]] (High-Temperature Superconductor) magnets, plasma physics, and artificial intelligence technologies to commercialize fusion energy. Using the funded capital, the company would develop an experimental [[tokamak]] device planned to be operational by 2024.<ref>{{Cite news |author=Energy Singularity |date=26 February 2022 |title=Energy Singularity Raises nearly RMB400 Million in Series Seed Funding to Develop Fusion Energy |url=https://www.energysingularity.cn/en/energy-singularity-raises-nearly-rmb400-million-in-series-seed-funding-to-develop-fusion-energy/ |access-date=12 August 2022 |website=energysingularity.cn |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124435/https://www.energysingularity.cn/en/energy-singularity-raises-nearly-rmb400-million-in-series-seed-funding-to-develop-fusion-energy/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 20 May 2022, miHoYo participated in a funding round for [[Orienspace|Oriental Space Technology (Shandong) Co., Ltd]]., which raised CNY 400 million. The company focuses on aerospace technology and would develop a launch vehicle and a reusable liquid oxygen and kerosene rocket engine using the raised funds. The plan was for the rocket to launch in mid-2023.<ref>{{Cite web |title=东方空间 |url=https://www.qixin.com/brand/53ed82cc-7f39-4915-99b3-444ebac2466b/7MPYImQP5jrjHNrFXnZMn9jE85NPTERNMasNHq0sk1R8rLUCHLrBywPoCFwTgVbr |access-date=14 August 2022 |website=Qixinbao |url-access=registration |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124437/https://www.qixin.com/brand/53ed82cc-7f39-4915-99b3-444ebac2466b/7MPYImQP5jrjHNrFXnZMn9jE85NPTERNMasNHq0sk1R8rLUCHLrBywPoCFwTgVbr |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Jones |first=Andrew |date=20 May 2022 |title=Chinese launch startup Orienspace raises $59.9 million in Series A round |url=https://spacenews.com/chinese-launch-startup-orienspace-raises-59-9-million-in-series-a-round/ |access-date=14 August 2022 |website=SpaceNews }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |author=游戏葡萄 |date=21 May 2022 |title=米哈游投资了一家民营火箭科技公司 |url=https://3g.163.com/dy/article/H7TFB1PL05268BP2.html |access-date=14 August 2022 |website=NetEase }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |author=Sina Finance |date=20 May 2022 |title=民营火箭东方空间完成4亿元A轮融资 |url=https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/2022-05-20/doc-imcwiwst8414660.shtml |access-date=14 August 2022 |website=Sina |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124434/https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/2022-05-20/doc-imcwiwst8414660.shtml |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Committees===
{{POV section|date=August 2023}}
In May 2021, miHoYo established the [[Communist Youth League of China|Communist Youth League]] Committee under Shanghai Mihoyo Network Technology Co., Ltd. The committee aims to integrate youth into company development and partake in the innovation and publicization of traditional Chinese culture. The committee created comics and travel maps with the help of ''Genshin Impact'' material to promote [[Xuhui District]] cultural tourism landmarks. The character Paimon was formally named "Xuhui Youth Culture Star Promoter."<ref>{{Cite web |author=疯鸭骑士 |date=23 May 2021 |title=米哈游《原神》IP派蒙成为"徐汇青年文化星推官" |url=https://www.bilibili.com/read/cv11397442/ |access-date=27 July 2022 |website=Bilibili |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124432/https://www.bilibili.com/read/cv11397442/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=米哈游团委成立 |url=https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100977 |access-date=29 July 2022 |website=mihoyo.com |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124435/https://www.mihoyo.com/m/news/100977 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In September 2021, Shanghai Mihoyo Network Technology Co., Ltd. got promoted from a party branch to a party committee under the [[Chinese Communist Party]] (CCP).<ref>{{Cite web |title=中国共产党上海米哈游网络科技股份有限公司委员会党员大会顺利召开 |url=https://www.mihoyo.com/news/100974 |access-date=6 July 2022 |website=mihoyo.com |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124433/https://www.mihoyo.com/news/100974 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 8 July 2022, Shanghai Mihoyo Network Technology Co., Ltd. had its first trade union congress. miHoYo vice president Yin Chunbo was elected as the chairman of the first session of miHoYo's trade union committee. The meeting stated MiHoYo's establishment of a trade union not only helps safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of employees, promotes the high-quality development of enterprises and industries, but also serves the economic development of trade union organizations.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=8 July 2022 |title=上海米哈游网络科技股份有限公司工会成立大会顺利召开！ |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/p0T1UjDS7Jg8xOVg9TA3tQ |access-date=31 July 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=7 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221007171202/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/p0T1UjDS7Jg8xOVg9TA3tQ |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Rankings and certification===
In August 2021, miHoYo Technology (Shanghai) Co., Ltd. was selected as a "Key National Cultural Export Enterprise" along with ''Genshin Impact'' as a "Key National Cultural Export Project" for the 2021-2022 period. Previously, the company and ''Honkai Impact 3rd'' was selected for those titles in 2019. The annual ''List of National Cultural Export Key Enterprises and Key Projects'' is organized by the offices of the [[Ministry of Commerce (China)|Ministry of Commerce]], [[Ministry of Finance of the People's Republic of China|Ministry of Finance]], [[Ministry of Culture and Tourism of the People's Republic of China|Ministry of Culture and Tourism]], and the [[Publicity Department of the Chinese Communist Party|Central Propaganda Department]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=米哈游再次入选国家文化出口重点企业 《原神》入选国家文化出口重点项目 |url=https://www.mihoyo.com/news/100593 |access-date=27 July 2022 |website=mihoyo.com |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124433/https://www.mihoyo.com/news/100593 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In August 2022, miHoYo obtained information security certifications for [[ISO/IEC 27001]] and [[ISO/IEC 27701]] issued by the [[British Standards Institution]] (BSI). According to miHoYo's official announcement published in October 2022, the company had "undergone a comprehensive assessment, including strict on-site audits."<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=11 October 2022 |title=米哈游正式通过ISO27001及ISO27701双重认证 |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/PE7H2V8iiRs-itBoLa-W3Q |access-date=20 November 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=20 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221120155523/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/PE7H2V8iiRs-itBoLa-W3Q |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 26 November 2021, the [[Internet Society of China]] released the China Internet Enterprise Comprehensive Strength Index ({{lang|zh|中国互联网企业综合实力指数}}) for 2021. miHoYo was listed as one of "China's Top 100 Internet Enterprises with Comprehensive Strength"; miHoYo ranked 23rd on the list, 1st among Shanghai game companies, and 3rd among Shanghai internet companies. It was also the fifth consecutive time miHoYo was included in the list.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=29 November 2021 |title=2021年中国互联网综合实力企业百强揭晓 米哈游连续五年上榜 |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/gvTERA2PK1yw9A2CZ5vZjw |access-date=31 July 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=26 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220826124439/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/gvTERA2PK1yw9A2CZ5vZjw |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 24 November 2022, the [[Shanghai Cultural and Creative Industry Promotion Association]] ({{lang|zh|上海市文化创意产业促进会}}) and [[Shanghai First Financial Media Co.]], Ltd. ({{lang|zh|上海第一财经传媒有限公司}})—under the guidance of the Shanghai Municipal Committee Propaganda Department—announced Shanghai Mihoyo Yingtie Technology Co., Ltd. as one of the Top Ten Cultural Enterprises, company co-founder [[Liu Wei (businessman, born 1987)|Liu Wei]] as one of the Top Ten People of the Year, and ''Genshin Impact'' as one of the Top Ten Cultural Brands of Shanghai.<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=24 November 2022 |title=米哈游荣获"上海文化企业十强" |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/MRKpyT7R3i3zNMlXeJxMoQ |access-date=19 December 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=18 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221218170032/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/MRKpyT7R3i3zNMlXeJxMoQ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |author=第一财经 |date=25 November 2022 |title=上海文化企业十强总营收破500亿！B站、米哈游等上榜 |url=https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/internet/2022-11-25/doc-imqqsmrp7490882.shtml |access-date=19 December 2022 |website=Sina Finance |archive-date=18 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221218170353/https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/internet/2022-11-25/doc-imqqsmrp7490882.shtml |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 28 December 2022, [[Guangming Daily]] and [[Economic Daily]] jointly announced the "Top 30 National Cultural Enterprises" with Shanghai Mihoyo Network Technology Co., Ltd. included in the list. miHoYo was praised by Guangming Daily as "a representative scientific and technological innovation enterprise driven by Shanghai's innovation and entrepreneurship policies."<ref>{{Cite news |author=米哈游 |date=29 December 2022 |title=米哈游荣获"全国文化企业30强" |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/M3e4___iq0XYGZicdLQ-iQ |access-date=31 December 2022 |website=Weixin |archive-date=31 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221231064023/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/M3e4___iq0XYGZicdLQ-iQ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |author=GameLook |date=30 December 2022 |title=米哈游获评"全国文化企业30强"：21年收入200亿、海外占一半 |url=http://www.gamelook.com.cn/2022/12/506793 |access-date=31 December 2022 |website=GameLook |archive-date=31 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221231065059/http://www.gamelook.com.cn/2022/12/506793 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In February 2023, during the [[2022 China Game Industry Annual Conference]] ({{lang|zh|2022年度中国游戏产业年会}}), hosted by the {{Ill|China Audio-Video and Digital Publishing Association|lt=China Audio-Video and Digital Publishing Association|zh|中国音像与数字出版协会}} and sponsored by the [[National Press and Publication Administration]] (NPPA),<ref>{{Cite web |author=每日经济新闻 |date=15 February 2023 |title=游戏产业年会观察⑤ 腾讯、网易、三七互娱、米哈游等龙头公司领头人交出2023目标"小作文" |url=https://www.nbd.com.cn/articles/2023-02-15/2669762.html |access-date=15 February 2023 |website=nbd.com.cn |archive-date=15 February 2023 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20230215145922/https://www.nbd.com.cn/articles/2023-02-15/2669762.html |url-status=live }}</ref> announced miHoYo as a recipient of two awards. The company was selected as one of the Top Ten "Going Global" Game Enterprises, and the game ''Genshin Impact'' as one of the Top Ten Outstanding Mobile Games. miHoYo and ''Genshin Impact'' were also nominated for several other awards.<ref>{{Cite web |author=米哈游 |date=15 February 2023 |title=米哈游荣获2022中国游戏十强优秀"走出去"游戏企业等奖项 |url=https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/2PMo8O5ojguSgOvZozJB7Q |access-date=15 February 2023 |website=Weixin |archive-date=15 February 2023 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20230215145649/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/2PMo8O5ojguSgOvZozJB7Q |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=中国音像与数字出版协会：2022年游戏十强年度榜公布 《王者荣耀》《原神》等上榜 |url=https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2023-02-14/doc-imyfsncq9231687.shtml |access-date=15 February 2023 |website=Weixin |date=14 February 2023 |archive-date=15 February 2023 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20230215150149/https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2023-02-14/doc-imyfsncq9231687.shtml |url-status=live }}</ref>

==HoYoverse==
[[File:HoYoverse Logo.svg|thumb|HoYoverse logo]]
[[File:Genshin_Impact_Teyvat_Goods_Store_Chicago_2026.jpg|thumb|The inside of the ''Genshin Impact'' Teyvat Goods pop-up store in [[Chicago]] in 2026.]]
Cognosphere Pte., Ltd. ({{lang-zh|s=识隙之城私人有限公司}}) stylized as COGNOSPHERE, and [[Trade name|doing business as]] HoYoverse, is a publishing company based in [[Singapore]]. Established in 2021, HoYoverse handles international distribution of miHoYo's games as well as the operation of community platform HoYoLAB.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Home {{!}} HoYoverse |url=https://www.hoyoverse.com/en-us/ |access-date=2024-07-10 |website=www.hoyoverse.com |language=en-us}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Square |first=Push |date=2023-09-26 |title=Preview: Genshin Impact, Honkai: Star Rail Dev Has Quietly Become a PS5, PS4 Powerhouse |url=https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2023/09/preview-genshin-impact-honkai-star-rail-dev-has-quietly-become-a-ps5-ps4-powerhouse |access-date=2024-07-10 |website=Push Square |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref name="hoyotechtimes">{{Cite web |last=Tejares |first=Sarah Mae |title=HoYoverse Announces Its Full Lineup for Gamescom 2023 |url=https://www.techtimes.com/articles/293658/20230711/pr-hoyoverse-announces-full-lineup-gamescom-2023.htm |archive-date= |access-date=2024-07-10 |website=techtimes.com|date=11 July 2023 }}</ref> The company has set up offices in Los Angeles, Montreal, Tokyo, and Seoul.<ref name="auto">{{Cite web |title=Presenting the New Brand HoYoverse: Aiming to Provide Global Players With an Immersive Virtual World Experience {{!}} HoYoverse |url=https://www.hoyoverse.com/en-us/news/101566 |access-date=2024-07-10 |website=www.hoyoverse.com |language=en-us}}</ref><ref name="auto1">{{Cite web |date=2022-07-18 |title=Genshin Impact makers HoYoverse open Singapore HQ, to hire 'hundreds' by end 2022 |url=https://sg.news.yahoo.com/genshin-impact-hoyoverse-singapore-headquarters-office-061049544.html |access-date=2024-07-10 |website=Yahoo News |language=en-GB}}</ref>

miHoYo promotes its merchandise in part by organizing [[pop-up retail]] stores in various cities around the world, including [[London]] and [[Chicago]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lada |first=Jenni |date=2025-02-13 |title=Genshin Impact Pop-Up Store Heads to London |url=https://www.siliconera.com/genshin-impact-pop-up-store-heads-to-london/ |access-date=2026-05-30 |website=Siliconera |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite tweet |number=2055839315553395115 |user=GenshinImpact |title=Hey Travelers, the Teyvat Goods Pop-Up Store is coming to Chicago! Don't miss this — it's happening from May 30 to June 7! |author=Genshin Impact |date=2026-05-16 |access-date=2026-05-30}}</ref>

